* LTspice version of the lane library: the same circuit as the .lib next to it, with Rser=0 Rpar=1e30 on every
* inductor (LTspice adds a series resistance of 1 mOhm and an implicit parallel damping to inductors by default)
* kisi 0.3.3: lane DATA as a SPICE subcircuit (ngspice, Xyce, LTspice, KiCad)
* board board.kicad_pcb
* subcircuit DATA_lane (single line)
* port 1 (a): DATA at U1.4 (transmitter end)
* port 2 (b): DATA at U2.2 (receiver end)
* track length 28.12 mm, delay 162.1 ps, reference 50.00 ohm per port
* model (compact): kisi's channel sections; lines as lossless-line cells (at least 3 per delay x 10.00 GHz): per cell
*   a lossless LC ladder (40 sections per wavelength: the delay) and the fitted Foster (R(f), L_int(f)) and Debye
*   (G(f), C(f)) networks lumped once; consecutive sections with the same model merged (0 merges); vias as kisi's
*   via ladder, parts with estimated parasitics, open stubs; coupled sections of a pair as even/odd chains between
*   ideal mode converters (E/F). Passive and causal by construction.
* check against kisi's S-parameters (same model): |dS21| <= 0.005129 dB to 1.5 x Nyquist (0.4545 dB to the top), largest |dS| 0.0006898 to 1.5 x Nyquist (0.1747 to the top)
* fits of the main line sections (each at least 10 % of the length): R 0.5148 %, X 0.01713 %, G 17.43 %, B 3.524 %; via ladders 0 %
* elements after flattening: 144 R, 158 L, 136 C, 0 sources; 0 RLGC sections, 11 lossless-line cells
* usage: X1 a b 0 DATA_lane   (the last port is the reference)
* stackup: 2 copper layers, 1.49 mm, er and tand at 1 GHz; from board file (layer by layer in the README)
*   layers (um): F.Cu 30 / 1430 er 4.42 tand 0.02 / B.Cu 30

